==Icelandic==
{{Icelandic declension kk sb 03 og 03a|vin|ur}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/vɪnʏr/}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} ''[[vinr]]''.

===Noun===
'''vinur''' {{m}}

# [[friend]]
#: ''Þú ert '''vinur''' minn.''
#:: You are my '''friend'''.
#: ''Þú ert góður '''vinur'''.''
#:: You are a good '''friend'''.
# {{context|colloquial|slang|lang=is}} [[mate]], [[lad]], an affectionate moniker for a close [[friend]] or [[pal]], especially used as a form of [[address]].
#: ''[[jæja|Jæja]] '''vinurinn''', ætli maður fari ekki að [[koma sér af stað]].''
#:: Well '''mate''', I guess you should [[get going]]?

====Synonyms====
* (''friend''): [[máti]], [[félagi]], [[kumpáni]]
* (''mate''): [[kallinn]], [[gaur]], [[kjellinn]]

